.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH elfshaker-explode 1  "elfshaker 1.0.0-rc1" "elfshaker Manual"
.SH NAME
elfshaker\-explode \- Materialize a pack\*(Aqs objects in the loose\-object store.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBelfshaker explode\fR [\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPACK\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Extracts every object in a pack into the data directory\*(Aqs loose object store. The pack remains in place, and no loose snapshot indexes are created.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show informational progress and diagnostic messages.
.TP
\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR \fI<PATH>\fR [default: elfshaker_data]
Use PATH as the data directory containing packs, indexes, loose objects, remotes, and HEAD. This does not change the working directory.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIPACK\fR>
Pack whose objects should be materialized.
